WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.157
Lab 2 connects one
disposable server for real,

2
00:00:03.157 --> 00:00:07.900
in a commercial test subscription in
the GCC tenant, never production.

3
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:12.687
The control node runs somewhere with a
managed identity, so no secret is stored.

4
00:00:12.687 --> 00:00:17.123
Prepare a resource group, grant the
onboarding role to that identity

5
00:00:17.123 --> 00:00:21.013
and nothing else, and describe
the one server in a tiny export.

6
00:00:21.013 --> 00:00:26.450
Then the same three commands every
wave uses: plan, dry run, connect.

7
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.453
Check the agent says connected,

8
00:00:28.453 --> 00:00:32.150
the tags match the database,
and the validation kit agrees.

9
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:35.450
Then back it out in Learn's
order, and file the records.
